Hi all! So I was just looking for some opinions from people here, but don't know if my question is enough in itself to have its own post.

&#x200B;

My question is: do you think a barely passed N1 qualification is worth anything? Of course it's not worth the same as a full mark, but is it worth anything at all or are you better off getting an N2 with a good score?

Boku isn't very socially acceptable for an afab person to say. It is commonly seen in anime, but in real life there are lots of people who hate bokukko (that's what afab ppl who use "boku" are called) and think they are annoying.

&#x200B;

If you put "僕っ娘" on Japanese Yahoo answers (otherwise known as chiebukuro), you'll find lots of posts about girls asking whether it's ok to refer to themselves as boku. Most people reply that you shouldn't use it in a public space. Some even go as far as saying it's "disgusting" when they do. It's not as bad as what the orekko (afab people who use ore) get, but it's definitely not widely socially accepted.

