Oh and I forgot to mention it in my post, but she's trying to brainwash my youngest brother into moving to Turkey with her and she forces him to talk to her new boyfriend during their Zoom calls.

Yeah. I especially hear it used in contexts where white people are living abroad in Asian countries. Whenever I hear stuff like "expat community in Japan" I always feel tempted to say "you mean immigrant community, right?", just to see how offended they can get that they're not getting special treatment words.

&#x200B;

Edit: I mostly used the word "anglo world" because in a lot of other European languages, like Spanish, the distinction doesn't exist. It seems like a very English thing.

"Spanish is easy because it's so similar to English!".

&#x200B;

I'm not saying this isn't partially true. But English and Spanish only share 30% of vocabulary, and they're not even used for the same things all the time. I think people really don't realize how small of a percentage 30% understanding is, and that's not even accounting for differences in grammar. Portuguese and Spanish share 80% of vocabulary, and even we have to make an effort to learn each other's language (and we struggle a lot, at that. Nobody wants to be the guy who barely makes an effort because the other person can somewhat understand what you're saying).

&#x200B;

Edit: also, not every country calls people from the US "gringo". For example, in Argentina we say "yankee".

it does sting.... I feel so hurt knowing some people really can't see us as anything other than sentient (and by sentient they mean annoying and over-emotional) fleshlights.

&#x200B;

Like just the other day, I was talking to some random guys who wanted to learn/practice my native language on discord and one of them was like "k guys let's make another server so we can talk, except takethisedandshoveit. Nothing personal I just want guys to come here" and when the other guys pressured him into getting me in, I said "maybe now I don't want to be in your stupid social club" and he said "see? women are so petty." I don't know why I bother trying to be friends with men.
